                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Play Time: 12.3hrs\nAchievements: 12 out of 12. 100%\nDate/Version: August 26th 2026\nRating: 7 out of 10\n\nIron Sea Defenders is a Tower Defense game that I would say is more designed around a casual TD Player base. Each map has 3 difficulties and many stages. These maps all have a different feel and theme to them. You have several DLC's you can purchase (see WARNING) that give you more tower defense fun, and there's even a workshop. Within the base game you have 4 primary base towers, and several sub towers. As well has some global skill that the user can use to impact the run. Now I have no idea of the workshop works, but it's there to click on. The options are very bare bone, and I'm not sure if they game is pure keyboard compatible. The achievements were great, and should be able to be obtained just via completing the game, and 3 staring (no hits received) the first main map on all difficulties. The game follows the typical 3 star rule, as in 0 hits to your tower is 3 star which will give you “anchors” to spend on meta game upgrades. Usually this can be annoying but I found the game not to be super difficult compared to other tower defense games I've played. Lastly you can use anchors to open up blocked tower spots, I think you can beat the hardest maps without opening them all up seeing as that's what I did at the highest difficulty setting on the first main map. I felt this was an enjoyable base line tower defense game, and a should buy for fans of the tower defense genre. \n\nWARNING: Many of the reviews indicate to not buy the DLC's as they can cause problems with your game. I don't have the DLC's and have no idea if these issues were ever fixed. \n\n(Potential Spoilers)\n\nUnits/towers:\n4 different towers, each with 2 different sub tower type you can utilize.\nThis offers a nice variety\n\n\n\nMeta/Skill progress: Linked to beating each scenario.\nThese were nice buffs not too powerful and not to weak.\nYou have meta buffs that reduce tower cost, increase damage, increase range, increase your global skill abilities, and increase your passives such as how much money you'll get per unit destroyed. \n\n\nAchievements:\n12 achievements that can be obtained just by playing the game and beating the first main map on all 3 difficulties perfectly. These were nice and thought they were a great balance. \n\nDifficulty:\nI felt it was fun, and not too difficult. A bit of puzzling goes a long way.\n\nFinal Thoughts:\nGet the game if you enjoy this aesthetic appeal and if you enjoy tower defense style games, especially if it's on sale. It's a great baseline for the Tower Defense genre and was enjoyable.",
